# The 2D scene, which F7 in mygame cycles to (see docs/rendering/2d.md#sprite-renderers): an orthographic camera that
# looks along +z at sprites in the xy plane. A hero walks over a row of tiles and plays its sheet's animations by name;
# coins spin; three cards overlap by their layers and orders, not by their depths; and of two rows of crates, the lit
# one takes the lamp's light and the unlit one shows its colors. A texel is 5 pixels at a height of 720, so the snapped
# sprites stay sharp. Positions are raw World_Position values in units of 2^-24 m. The editor writes this file; see
# docs/editor/document-and-scenes.md#scenes.
scene 2

